  "title": "5 Signs You Talk More Than You Ask (And the One Fix) #shorts",
  "description": "How many did you check? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who checks all five. Otto talked through the whole lunch and thinks it went great. In 'It doesn't hurt to ask: Question-asking increases liking' (Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 2017), Karen Huang, Michael Yeomans, Alison Wood Brooks, Julia Minson and Francesca Gino studied online chats and speed dates: people who asked more questions, especially follow-up questions, were liked more by their partners, and on speed dates question-askers got more second dates. Being interesting isn't the trick; being interested is. Ask 'then what happened?' #psychology #shorts #conversation #likability #overthinking",
